dhp316:1 starts: Ashamed of what’s not shameful,
dhp316:2 starts: not ashamed of what is,
dhp316:3 starts: beings adopting wrong views
dhp316:4 starts: go to a bad destination.
dhp335:1 starts: If this sticky, uncouth craving
dhp335:2 starts: overcomes you in the world,
dhp335:3 starts: your sorrows grow like wild grass
dhp335:4 starts: after rain.
dhp322:1 starts: Excellent are tamed mules,
dhp322:2 starts: tamed horses from Sindh.
dhp322:3 starts: Excellent, tamed tuskers,
dhp322:4 starts: But even more excellent
dhp336:1 starts: If, in the world, you overcome
dhp336:2 starts: this uncouth craving, hard to escape,
dhp336:3 starts: sorrows roll off you,
dhp336:4 starts: like water beads off
dhp337:1 starts: To all of you gathered here
dhp337:2 starts: I say: Good fortune.
dhp337:3 starts: Dig up craving
dhp337:4 starts: –as when seeking medicinal roots, wild grass–
dhp337:5 starts: Don’t let Mara cut you down
dhp337:6 starts: a reed–
dhp338:1 starts: If its root remains
dhp338:2 starts: a tree, even if cut,
dhp338:3 starts: So too if craving-obsession
dhp338:4 starts: this suffering returns
dhp339:1 starts: He whose 36 streams,
dhp339:2 starts: flowing to what is appealing, are strong:
dhp339:3 starts: the currents–resolves based on passion–
dhp339:4 starts: carry him, of base views, away.
dhp341:1 starts: Loosened & oiled
dhp341:2 starts: are the joys of a person.
dhp341:3 starts: People, bound by enticement,
dhp341:4 starts: to birth & aging they go.
dhp342:1 starts: Encircled with craving,
dhp342:2 starts: hop round & around
dhp342:3 starts: Tied with fetters & bonds
dhp342:4 starts: they go on to suffering,
dhp343:1 starts: Encircled with craving,
dhp343:2 starts: like a rabbit caught in a snare.
dhp343:3 starts: So a monk
dhp343:4 starts: should dispel craving,
dhp348:1 starts: Gone to the beyond of becoming,
dhp348:2 starts: you let go of in front,
dhp348:3 starts: With a heart everywhere released,
dhp348:4 starts: you don’t come again to birth
dhp366:1 starts: Even if he gets next to nothing,
dhp366:2 starts: he doesn’t treat his gains with scorn.
dhp366:3 starts: Living purely, untiring:
dhp366:4 starts: he’s the one
dhp367:1 starts: For whom, in name & form
dhp367:2 starts: there’s no sense of mine,
dhp367:3 starts: & who doesn’t grieve
dhp367:4 starts: he’s deservedly called
